{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74-brief.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Council round 74: review the slice-1 build design before any code (read-only)\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n     4\t\n     5\t## What to review\n     6\t\n     7\t`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`, the build design for the first slice of the \"Forecast unavailable\"\n     8\trelease. The governing documents:\n     9\t- `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4, ready per `codex-r72d.md`);\n    10\t- D726, D756, D757 and D758 at the end of `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`;\n    11\t- AGENTS.md §2 (design tables before code), §3 (one owner; the writer refuses), §4 (tests) and §5.\n    12\t\n    13\tCode that the design reuses:\n    14\t- `src/hivemind/service.py`: `resolve_bound`, `view_exists`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `evidence`, `evidence_record`,\n    15\t  `ladder_bands`;\n    16\t- `src/hivemind/bundle.py`: `read_snapshot`, `item_lookup`, `view_bundle`;\n    17\t- `src/hivemind/views/store.py`: `view_key`, `rungs_of`;\n    18\t- `src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10`;\n    19\t- `src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24`;\n    20\t- `src/hivemind/idea.py`, for the idea question.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Questions\n    23\t\n    24\t1. **Leaks.** Does the allow-list in §1 let any number forecast reach the package? Check:\n    25\t   - each allowed field's real content in stored stores, read-only (for example `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`):\n    26\t     `question`, evidence `one_line` and `quote`, source titles;\n    27\t   - whether evidence linked to a number question can itself be a system-written forecast rather than a source statement.\n    28\t\n    29\t   Name any path with a stored example.\n    30\t2. **Tables.** Are the state × event, value × reader and new path × old checks tables complete? Name any blank or wrong cell, for\n    31\t   example an event the export can meet that is not listed.\n    32\t3. **Tests and mutants.** Does each named test fail without the code it tests? Is a decisive case missing?\n    33\t4. **The $0 release check (§7).** Is the leak sweep sound? Consider the 12-character floor and the string classes. Would it miss a\n    34\t   forecast restated in different words?\n    35\t5. **The four open points in §8:**\n    36\t   - no idea submission in the release, with the idea acceptance moved to a later slice;\n    37\t   - `object` and `kind` on every record;\n    38\t   - groups left out;\n    39\t   - the sweep floor.\n    40\t\n    41\t   Decide each.\n    42\t6. **Ready to build?** Give a verdict: ready, or not ready with each serious finding.\n    43\t\n    44\t**Out of scope:** the judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen); the closed v13s line; the POC's own behaviour; any other open\n    45\tdefect; wording. Report only findings that change what is built or whether it is safe.\n     1\t**Not ready to build.** Both 74h findings are closed. One case remains undefined for `check`: a valid package in a readable directory where the command cannot write its report.\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Cleanup after publication is closed.** Once the link succeeds, the report is published. If removing the temporary file then fails, the command exits 0 and names the leftover file. Test 20 forces that exact failure and verifies the published report’s contents. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:381](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:381)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **The end-to-end exit statuses are closed.** Test 11 requires `check` to print a pass and exit 2 while the build’s report exists, then exit 0 and create a fresh report after the test removes it. Test 19 requires exit 2 and verifies that the file which took the report name survives unchanged. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:351](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:351) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:378](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:378)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **Remaining blocker: `check` has no specified exit status for other report-write failures.** Suppose the package passes, the report name is free, and creating the temporary file fails with `EACCES`. None of the three listed outcomes fits. `build` already assigns exit 2 to every report failure before the link succeeds. Apply that same rule to `check`. The decisive test forces the temporary-file creation to fail after validation and requires a printed pass, the write error, and exit 2. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:206](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:206) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:211)\n     8\t\n     9\tI found no other serious blocker in slice 1.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
