{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files --hidden --no-ignore poc/data | rg '(views|items[\"'^/]*)'\"\\\\.sqlite\"'$'\"' | rg 'run/old|items-comparison|served' | head -40; rg -n 'served ledger|served.*sqlite' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74*.md | head -14\"","aggregated_output":"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md:11:| **5. Diagnostic columns** | **Closed.** The two optional judgement columns are read only where present, and the report records their absence. I verified that the served ledger has `reasons` and `why_changed` and lacks both `implied_outcome` and `reference`. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:339](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:339) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:5:I checked the three comparison stores and the served ledger read-only. I found **no confirmed case of a stored judgement being copied into an evidence record**. I did find a meaningful difference between the article, the system’s summary of it, and the system’s own answer. The build design treats all three as strings.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:33:- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restriction adopted.”** All 85 comparison-store events also have Yes/No labels, so removing event recognition can leave the displayed answer unchanged. Exercise the legacy case with the key table genuinely absent. [Tests:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:168) · [Event overlap:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Legacy lookup:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:159)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:16:**Claude is right about what the production extraction request sees.** For an existing question, it sends the ID, object, due day, question and a description of what evidence belongs there. It sends no stored rung, rung label or judged position. The response schema asks the model to *write* labels for newly proposed questions. `research_context.Reader` really does load stored rungs and the latest judgement, but its expanded record is not sent by `extraction.read_item`. I also checked the historical archive because the served ledger used extraction v18. Across its 1,819 extraction requests, the 43,895 displayed thesis lines contained the ID, object, focus, due day and question. [placement.py:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/placement.py:19) · [placement.py:59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/placement.py:59) · [extraction.py:399](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:399) · [extraction.py:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:88) · [extraction.py:460](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:460) · [research_context.py:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/research_context.py:49) · [research_context.py:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/research_context.py:95) · [README.md:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/README.md:114)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:28:5. **Make the four-store acceptance runnable.** Step 7 asks for `judgements.implied_outcome` and `reference` on every store. I checked the served ledger’s actual schema. It has neither column. Read the available diagnostic columns and report the two as absent on that ledger. Otherwise the specified acceptance can fail on a valid package before it finishes. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:261) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:285](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:285) · [store.py:152](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:152)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
