{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'served-2026-10-28|items.*sqlite' README.md | head -14; rg -n '\"'^## [2-5]'\"\\\\.' AGENTS.md; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10991,11010p'\"","aggregated_output":"93:| Collected thesis ledger | `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` |\n94:| Source items | `poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite` (cleaned pages, D351, with the whole pages as fetched in column `text_page`; also kept apart in `items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.page.sqlite`) |\n110:| `docker-compose.yml` | the `/data/ledger` and `/data/items/items-window.sqlite` volumes of both services |\n114:Then restart the API in a new dated service folder (below) so the search index is built for the new ledger. The current default, `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828`, is the three-month NVDA run (`poc-v34`, extraction v18) stopped and sealed at 2026-08-28 on evidence bloat (D358); its folder README names the one empty thesis removed.\n160:  --items \"$repo/poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\"\n170:`--cap` is checked after each item: parallel calls already sent and the day's judging round can exceed it, so it is not a hard whole-run limit. The default is `poc-v118`; the default input database is `poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite`. A ledger containing the retired seeded questions is refused. Earnings releases still enter as actual source items; a report is not appended as background to other items. The new replay default is not accepted end to end. The historical seeded judgement scorer requires its frozen seeds and therefore is not a valid scorer for the new no-seed run. The [pipeline guide](docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md) describes the stages.\n91:## 2. Before writing code: design\n122:## 3. Writing code\n145:## 4. Tests\n168:## 5. Verification\n 10991\t## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n 10992\t\n 10993\t- **The questions** (after D725):\n 10994\t  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n 10995\t    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n 10996\t    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n 10997\t  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n 10998\t    (recommended); 暂不定.\n 10999\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n 11000\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11001\t  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n 11002\t    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n 11003\t    ceiling.\n 11004\t  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n 11005\t    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n 11006\t- poc-v118 stays the product.\n 11007\t\n 11008\t## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\n 11009\t\n 11010\t- **Design:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md`, v1 to v9. Council rounds 46 to 46e reached READY FOR THE $0 GATE on v5.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
