{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"**Ready to build slice 1.** The 74i finding is closed. I found no other serious blocker in revision 10.\n\n1. **`check` now has a defined outcome for the missing case.** If the package passes but creating the temporary report file raises `PermissionError`, `check` prints the pass and the write error, then exits 2. Test 21 requires all three. The same exit rule covers any failure before the report link succeeds. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:68](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:68) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:214](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:214) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:385](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:385)\n2. **The package checks are specific enough to implement.** I verified the stored example used for acceptance. Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate and the system’s own “About $390 billion” forecast are both present in `old-1`. The design requires the first to survive export and requires the checker to reject the second if it is substituted into Morningstar’s summary. The builder must run that check before publishing the package. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:154](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:154) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:437](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:437)"}}
